hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"20958","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Ata ibn al-Saib informed us from Bilal ibn Yaqtur that a man from the companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was appointed over Sijistan, and a man from the companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, met him and said: Do you remember the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he appointed a man over an army, and with him was a kindled fire, and he said to a man of his companions: Stand and jump into it. So he stood and approached it, and that reached the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so he said: Had he fallen into it they would both have entered the Fire. There is no obedience in disobedience of Allah, blessed and exalted. I only wanted to remind you of this. And Hammad also said: Stand and jump into it, so he refused, and he insisted upon him. And Hammad also said: No obedience in disobedience of Allah, exalted. He said: Yes."
"20973","Affan narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated to us, Ammar, meaning Ibn Abi Ammar, informed us from Ibn Abbas who said: A time came upon me when I said: The children of the Muslims are with the Muslims, and the children of the polytheists are with the polytheists, until so-and-so narrated to me from so-and-so that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was asked about them and said: Allah knows what they would have done. He said: I met the man and he informed me, so I withheld my saying."
